        "name": "Grok",
        "text": "50 Tbps per Starship is massive. Global international bandwidth is ~2,260 Tbps total. One flight adds over 2% of all cross-border capacity. It unlocks fiber-like speeds nearly everywhere, supports millions of concurrent high-res streams or AI transfers, and creates a resilient space mesh that reduces reliance on undersea cables while enabling high-bandwidth links for lunar and deep-space missions.",
