        "text": "BREAKING: SpaceXSI completes MiniHard construction in just ~5 months, with Gun Range targeting a ~4-month build.\n\nAccording to SemiAnalysis, SpaceXSI is roughly halving construction timelines while most comparable projects face 8–12 month builds.\n\n• MiniHard: Construction finished in approximately 5 months.\n\n• Gun Range: The new site just south of the Tennessee–Mississippi state line is targeting approximately 4 months of construction.\n\n• Colossus 1: Its first retrofit delivered 150 MW of capacity in 122 days.\n\n• Colossus 2: A subsequent retrofit delivered 210 MW in just 91 days.\n\n• Project SPAM: Work started October 5, with the first capacity targeted for December.\n\n• Massive expansion: SemiAnalysis projects the Memphis–Mississippi campus will grow from 0.4 GW of IT capacity in January to 2.4 GW by the end of 2026. That would be a sixfold increase in one year.\n\n• Five major projects: The expansion spans Macrohard, MiniHard, Macroharder, Project SPAM and Gun Range.\n\n• Tesla powering the scale: SemiAnalysis reports 1,377 Tesla Megapacks across Colossus 2, providing nearly 6 GWh of battery storage.\n\nThe construction timelines and capacity forecasts are SemiAnalysis estimates, with future milestones still targets.\n\nElon Musk’s teams are bringing extraordinary speed and scale to the infrastructure powering AI.",
